>> title: Harvest Chopped Salad
>> category: Salads
>> tags: kale, squash, pecans, apple, goat cheese
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: fall harvest chopped, harvest salad, autumn chopped salad, fall salad, squash and kale salad, chopped kale salad
>> pairs-with: basic-vinaigrette
>> servings: 4
>> time: 50 min
>> slack: forgiving — every component holds a day in the fridge separately, and the salad is twenty seconds of tossing at the end

Preheat the #oven{} to 425°F (220°C).

>> step: roast 425°F 25 min
Roast @delicata squash{1%lb}(450 g; halved, seeded, sliced in 1/2-in half-moons) with @extra-virgin olive oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL) and @kosher salt{1/2%tsp} on a #sheet pan{} for ~roast{25%min}, cut side down and not moved for the first fifteen.

>> step: toast 6 min, cool hard
Toast @pecans{1%cup}(110 g) with @maple syrup{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @kosher salt{1/4%tsp} and @cayenne{1/8%tsp} in a #skillet{} over medium heat for ~toast{6%min}, then spread them on parchment to ~cool{10%min} in a single layer.

>> step: rub 1 min
Rub @lacinato kale{1%bunch}(stemmed, chopped in 1/2-in pieces) with @kosher salt{1/4%tsp} and @apple cider vinegar{1%Tbs}(15 mL) for ~rub{1%min}.

>> step: chop in
Chop @honeycrisp apple{1%large}(cored, in 1/2-in dice), @celery{2%ribs}(sliced thin) and @dried cranberries{1/3%cup} into @&(~1)kale{}.

>> step: toss
Toss @&(~1)chopped salad{} with @&(~4)roasted squash{}, @&(~3)candied pecans{}, @goat cheese{3%oz}(85 g; crumbled) and @basic vinaigrette{1/3%cup}(80 mL) while the squash is still warm.

Warm squash against cold vinaigrette is the feel of it. Dressed cold it is the same things and a duller plate.
